sform the data I guess using  some kind of importer like asimp you  could roll your own whatever but the  fact is all of this processing that  you're doing doesn't really need to be  done because what's the point of opening  a file reading the parts that you need  and then changing them into some other  data structure or layout so for example  it might be extracting all of the vertex  positions all of the vertex normals  everything you need loading up buffers  and then sending that to your GPU as  like a Vertex buffer why would you do  that every single time you launch your  game clearly you're trying to get to the  same end result every time so why don't  you just do that processing ahead of  time and that way if you ship your game  with those assets already processed then  it is literally as simple as just read  the data from disk and into CPU memory  or read the vertex bar buffer data from  disk into GPU memory like that is that's  all you need to do because it's already  perfect it's already in the format you  want it to be so those are kind of the  two reasons why you might want your own  3D model format it's the same kind of  situation with textures for textures we  typically store like the master assets  as like a PNG or a JPEG maybe both of  those are compressed formats PNG  technically doesn't have to be  compressed but it usually is which means  that every time we read it we have to  decode it we have to go through and  process all those pixels decode the data  and then we might actually need to  compress it into a different format such  as like a GPU texture compression format  and then send it to the GPU that's so  much extra work for literally no reason  there might be some further processing  that needs to be done such as custom  filtering MIP maps for whatever reason a  great example of that might be for like  environment Maps you don't want to just  have your GPU linearly filter everything  you want to use a custom filtering  sampling algorithm that 