  but otherwise you might notice there's  no 3D models there's nothing it's  there's just an asset pack and that  asset pack contains like literally all  of the assets except for sounds all of  the audio assets are inside this sound  bank and there's also an audio commands  range this will probably likely also be  combined into the asset pack in the  future but because we have Jay working  on audio and he kind of started this  system before I started the whole asset  back system it was just a lot easier for  this game at least to just ship them as  two separate systems like this and this  asset packed file if we just open up  like a hex editor is just a bunch of  binary data you can see it has this  header age that AP Hazel asset pack and  manages binary data and it starts with  like an index and then it literally just  has the binary data for like everything  else now if you guys are interested I  might make an in-depth video talking  about like how this works on a technical  level and all of the details drop a  comment below if you'd like to see that  but otherwise all of the assets are just  inside this single file you can build  one of these from hazelnut Hazel's  editor by just going file build asset  pack and it will automatically build  this single file with all of the assets  that are actually referenced by your  scene so if you have a bunch of assets  that you don't even use it's going to  skip all of those all of the assets that  are actually used inside your scenes and  inside your game they will be packaged  over here and when you actually launch  the games if we just launch dichotomy  you'll see over here in the bottom we  like for the first I think eight seconds  or so it shows this right and then after  a while it goes away if we open it again  here it is and it says the version of  the binary as well as the version of the  asset pack and they're separate because  obviously like the asset pack is  separate to that executable binary of  the actual like game application and you  can kind of update them separately  completely and you might want to see  what version of issue on if we just  launch this again you might notice that  this number is pretty big it's actually  the date and time so here we have like  the year the month the day and then the  time in like 24 hour times like 407 pm  and the reason it's like this is because  this is very very useful when you're  actually shipping this because you know  exactly when you built this so therefore  what version am I shipping like what is  this asset pack when was it built so I  really like having this instead of just  like some kind of arbitrary incrementing  version like we do currently for the  actual executable binary builds now the  other thing you might notice is that  other kind of binary the other dll we  had here asimp this is gone we don't  need it anymore because everything you  see here all of the 3D models like these  things which are actually skeletal  animations that's entirely using Hazel's  own model format that has nothing to do  with asimp and it's already in that  perfect like data layout where we can  just read it from disk and we have  everything we need so for example like  the entire node hierarchy all of the  bones all of the stuff we need to know  for that that sub mesh transforms all of  that can just be copied directly into  like a CPU size struct and then all the  vertex buffers and index buffers are  also just stored as is on disk so we can  just kind of stream them in basically  directly 2 GPU memory and that's it and  the performance gains of that are just  huge in fact I might make a video  talking about the performance of this  specifically because I think it's just  such a useful thing to do and it seems  obvious but I don't know maybe some of  you haven't even thought of making your  own three model format so yeah highly  recommend now the second major feature  that we shipped with  what's that what's the time it's oh wow  I've been recording for a long time huh  guess you guys will just have to wait  till the next devlog soz maybe uh maybe  download Hazel while you're waiting and  then you'll see

